WEBVTT

00:00:08,720 --> 00:00:13,720
Should I be taking methylcobolamine B12 as a cancer patient?

00:00:15,720 --> 00:00:18,720
In general, no, you shouldn't.

00:00:18,720 --> 00:00:22,720
So methylcobolamine is a form of B12.

00:00:22,720 --> 00:00:26,720
So remember, the main forms of B12 out there are

00:00:26,720 --> 00:00:30,720
the inorganic form called cyanocobolamine,

00:00:30,720 --> 00:00:34,720
which is not good and I don't recommend for anybody.

00:00:34,720 --> 00:00:36,720
Then you got hydroxylcobolamine

00:00:36,720 --> 00:00:41,720
and adenosylcobolamine, which don't have methyl groups.

00:00:41,720 --> 00:00:45,720
Or it's bound to a methyl group and it's called methylcobolamine.

00:00:45,720 --> 00:00:49,720
So these are all forms of B12.

00:00:49,720 --> 00:00:54,720
Well, I heard that people should be taking methylcobolamine

00:00:54,720 --> 00:00:58,720
because that helps with the MTHF or gene defect.

00:00:58,720 --> 00:01:02,720
Well, yeah, it can help with the MTHF or gene defect.

00:01:02,720 --> 00:01:06,720
But if you have cancer,

00:01:06,720 --> 00:01:09,720
methyl groups can silence tumor spressor genes

00:01:09,720 --> 00:01:15,720
so they can block the intrinsic apoptonic pathway,

00:01:15,720 --> 00:01:18,720
meaning that inside the cell,

00:01:18,720 --> 00:01:23,720
you have a pathway stimulated by what are called tumor suppressor genes

00:01:23,720 --> 00:01:27,720
that will stimulate cell death when a cancer,

00:01:27,720 --> 00:01:30,720
when a cell is going to rapid replication.

00:01:30,720 --> 00:01:34,720
AKA is being cancerous.

00:01:34,720 --> 00:01:39,720
So when you got a cell that's acting as its cancer,

00:01:39,720 --> 00:01:42,720
meaning it's rapidly replicating,

00:01:42,720 --> 00:01:45,720
your tumor suppressor gene should kick it and kill the cell.

00:01:45,720 --> 00:01:48,720
Well, methyl groups block that,

00:01:48,720 --> 00:01:52,720
methyl groups attached to that gene and turn that gene off.

00:01:52,720 --> 00:01:55,720
So it allows for the cancer to continue to grow.

00:01:55,720 --> 00:01:59,720
So cancer patients should not be taking methylfolate.

00:01:59,720 --> 00:02:02,720
You'll see that a label is methyl-tenterhydrofolate

00:02:02,720 --> 00:02:04,720
or methylfolate,

00:02:04,720 --> 00:02:08,720
or they should not be taking methylcobolamine.

00:02:08,720 --> 00:02:14,720
The only exception to that is if a person has a blood test,

00:02:14,720 --> 00:02:17,720
elevated homocysteine.

00:02:17,720 --> 00:02:20,720
So if a person has normal homocysteine levels

00:02:20,720 --> 00:02:22,720
and they have a diagnosis of cancer,

00:02:22,720 --> 00:02:25,720
they should not be taking excess methyl groups.

00:02:25,720 --> 00:02:30,720
If they have, well, what if they have an MTHFR defect?

00:02:30,720 --> 00:02:32,720
It doesn't make any difference.

00:02:32,720 --> 00:02:36,720
If you have cancer and you have a normal homocysteine,

00:02:36,720 --> 00:02:39,720
you should not be taking methylfolate,

00:02:39,720 --> 00:02:43,720
nor should you be taking methylcobolamine.

00:02:43,720 --> 00:02:47,720
Well, then they're not detoxified because the MTHFR gene

00:02:47,720 --> 00:02:49,720
has got defects on it.

00:02:49,720 --> 00:02:50,720
No, no.

00:02:50,720 --> 00:02:54,720
So does the MTHFR gene help with detoxification?

00:02:54,720 --> 00:02:55,720
Yes.

00:02:55,720 --> 00:02:58,720
There's a lot of other detox pathways.

00:02:58,720 --> 00:03:03,720
Taking excess methyl groups are going to silence genes.

00:03:03,720 --> 00:03:05,720
They're also going to do other things, too.

00:03:05,720 --> 00:03:10,720
So you never just recommend any practitioners are listening.

00:03:10,720 --> 00:03:15,720
You never just recommend methyl groups

00:03:15,720 --> 00:03:19,720
because the person has an MTHFR gene defect.

00:03:19,720 --> 00:03:21,720
You have to look at all the genes.

00:03:21,720 --> 00:03:24,720
If you have an MTHFR gene defect,

00:03:24,720 --> 00:03:26,720
and they're bioptored pathway,

00:03:26,720 --> 00:03:30,720
you're going to strongly push that pathway as well.

00:03:30,720 --> 00:03:33,720
You could have all sorts of mood issues as well.

00:03:33,720 --> 00:03:38,720
Only caveat to that is if a person has excess homocysteine,

00:03:38,720 --> 00:03:42,720
then we're going to have to take methyl groups for a short period of time.

